# Statements the replay is expected to refuse, and why each one is harmless.
#
# `migrations/` holds two kinds of file and this is the seam between them.
#
# The eight files numbered 20260901000100–000800 are **desired state**. They
# have been edited in place for a year, so each one already contains the effect
# of migrations that were applied to production later — `classmates.sql`
# creates its helpers in `private` today, and production created them in
# `public` and moved them a week afterwards.
#
# The ten files numbered 20260907–20260911 are **history**, recovered from
# `supabase_migrations.schema_migrations` on 21 September and byte-for-byte
# what production ran. `MIGRATION-HISTORY.md` step 2 is why they may not be
# edited: the point of them is that the file and the row agree.
#
# Replay the second kind on top of the first and ten statements ask for
# something that has already happened. Eight of the ten recovered migrations
# replay clean; these two do not, and every refusal below is the same fault in
# two shapes — a `set schema` for a function already moved, or a `create
# policy` for a policy already split.
#
# **They are refusals, not differences.** The end state was measured three ways
# and the three agree: the repaired file set, `schema.snapshot.sql`, and a live
# read of production all give the same md5 for every column, every constraint
# and every policy. The control matters as much as the check — the base eight
# alone, and the whole directory in filename order, both give different md5s,
# so the fingerprint is not one that says "same" to everything.
#
# This file is what stops that becoming a licence. `check.sh` applies the two
# files below without stopping on error and then requires the errors to be
# *exactly* this list: an eleventh refusal, or one of these with different
# wording, fails the run. Anything else applies under ON_ERROR_STOP as before.
#
# Format: <migration filename>|<the ERROR text, verbatim>

20260907134823_harden_security_definer_helpers.sql|function public.verified_student() does not exist
20260907134823_harden_security_definer_helpers.sql|function public.classmate(uuid) does not exist
20260907134823_harden_security_definer_helpers.sql|function public.in_class(text, text) does not exist
20260907134823_harden_security_definer_helpers.sql|function public.rls_auto_enable() does not exist
20260907141019_rls_initplan_and_policy_overlap.sql|policy "join your own classes" for table "enrollments" already exists
20260907141019_rls_initplan_and_policy_overlap.sql|policy "change your own enrollment" for table "enrollments" already exists
20260907141019_rls_initplan_and_policy_overlap.sql|policy "leave your own classes" for table "enrollments" already exists
20260907141019_rls_initplan_and_policy_overlap.sql|policy "create your own profile" for table "profiles" already exists
20260907141019_rls_initplan_and_policy_overlap.sql|policy "edit your own profile" for table "profiles" already exists
20260907141019_rls_initplan_and_policy_overlap.sql|policy "delete your own profile" for table "profiles" already exists
